                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9dd77729-9f5d-3061-925d-492256013bb7",
                        "entry_id": "777b7d71-e06a-31c4-9b86-f9e9436385ac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An early type of harmonica with metal plates enclosing free reeds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c89d75a7-4cbf-45ba-a5bd-6433bcae7c71",
                                "sense_id": "9dd77729-9f5d-3061-925d-492256013bb7",
                                "text": "When in the 18th century, European organ-builders, acousticians, physicists, etc., heard this remarkable free reed, they obviously were fascinated by it for a wealth of free reed instruments appeared in the early 19th century. These instruments varied in size and type. Some were portable, small and mouth-blown like the “blow accordion,” harmonica, aeolina, and symphonion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec2d165b-1244-4d32-8ab6-4c08e54a05b3",
                                "sense_id": "9dd77729-9f5d-3061-925d-492256013bb7",
                                "text": "Organ-builders were early on the scene in the eighteenth century, but soon there were the first mouth-blown instruments such as the aeolian or aeolina, which was a simple set of free reeds mounted side by side."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "558addcb-fc58-4ce1-b43f-ab4560497c65",
                                "sense_id": "9dd77729-9f5d-3061-925d-492256013bb7",
                                "text": "Aeolinas and aeolodicons were similar to the more popular physharmonica, a four-octave keyboard instrument with free reeds invented by Anton Haeckl of Vienna."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "246e4e34-8c3c-4a70-9052-cbf885e334ef",
                                "sense_id": "9dd77729-9f5d-3061-925d-492256013bb7",
                                "text": "The principle applied to the aeolina was of a series of small springs fitted in apertures in a metallic plate, which vibrated when breathed over."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
